From f97ecc2b105cfc11ce366f2ace44eb292a489646 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: PePe Amengual <2208324+jamengual@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 15:10:03 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: deliver SIGILL, not SIGBUS, for SME access traps

On CPUs that implement SME, instructions of the Scalable Matrix
Extension trap with exception class 0x1d when SME is not enabled.
do_el0_sync() had no case for it, so the trap fell through to the
default case and the process got SIGBUS (BUS_OBJERR).  Code that probes
for SME by executing an instruction expects SIGILL, as for any
unsupported instruction (and as Linux delivers when it does not support
SME): OpenSSL's capability detection, for example, catches SIGILL during
its probes, so programs embedding it (Node.js) died at startup.

Define EXCP_SME and treat it like an undefined instruction.  Seen with
an Apple M6 (FEAT_SME) host running FreeBSD as a guest.
---
 sys/arm64/arm64/trap.c     | 11 +++++++++++
 sys/arm64/include/armreg.h |  1 +
 2 files changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sys/arm64/arm64/trap.c b/sys/arm64/arm64/trap.c
index 867e5c57f..e3374df13 100644
--- a/sys/arm64/arm64/trap.c
+++ b/sys/arm64/arm64/trap.c
@@ -743,6 +743,17 @@ do_el0_sync(struct thread *td, struct trapframe *frame)
 		call_trapsignal(td, SIGILL, ILL_ILLOPN, (void *)frame->tf_elr,
 		    exception);
 		break;
+	case EXCP_SME:
+		/*
+		 * SME is not supported, so its instructions trap.  Treat them
+		 * like undefined instructions (as Linux does without SME):
+		 * code that probes for SME by executing an instruction, such
+		 * as OpenSSL's capability detection, expects SIGILL and dies
+		 * on the SIGBUS of the default case on CPUs that have SME.
+		 */
+		call_trapsignal(td, SIGILL, ILL_ILLTRP, (void *)frame->tf_elr,
+		    exception);
+		break;
 	case EXCP_SP_ALIGN:
 		call_trapsignal(td, SIGBUS, BUS_ADRALN, (void *)frame->tf_sp,
 		    exception);
diff --git a/sys/arm64/include/armreg.h b/sys/arm64/include/armreg.h
index 271fe693c..fb3e62321 100644
--- a/sys/arm64/include/armreg.h
+++ b/sys/arm64/include/armreg.h
@@ -671,6 +671,7 @@
 #define	 EXCP_MSR		0x18	/* MSR/MRS trap */
 #define	 EXCP_SVE		0x19	/* SVE trap */
 #define	 EXCP_FPAC		0x1c	/* Faulting PAC trap */
+#define	 EXCP_SME		0x1d	/* SME trap */
 #define	 EXCP_INSN_ABORT_L	0x20	/* Instruction abort, from lower EL */
 #define	 EXCP_INSN_ABORT	0x21	/* Instruction abort, from same EL */ 
 #define	 EXCP_PC_ALIGN		0x22	/* PC alignment fault */
